; kick-check: after a boot from a kickstart with the Rust
; virtioscsi.device in place of the C one, on a copy of the system disk.
; Unit 0 is the system disk: vscsitest runs on units 1-5 only.
FailAt 30
MakeDir SHARED:vscsi/kick >NIL:
Version virtioscsi.device FULL >SHARED:vscsi/kick/version.txt
Type SHARED:vscsi/kick/version.txt
; Reads from the system disk through the Rust driver.
CD SYS:Libs
C:MD5Sum #? >SHARED:vscsi/kick/libs.md5
CD RAM:
; Writes to the system disk (the copy), read back.
MakeDir DH0:rusttest >NIL:
Copy SYS:Libs DH0:rusttest ALL QUIET
CD DH0:rusttest
C:MD5Sum #? >SHARED:vscsi/kick/dh0copy.md5
CD RAM:
Delete DH0:rusttest ALL QUIET FORCE >NIL:
; The test units.
Copy SHARED:vscsi/dropin/vscsitest RAM: QUIET
Protect RAM:vscsitest +rwed QUIET
RAM:vscsitest virtioscsi.device 6 6 1 >SHARED:vscsi/kick/vscsitest.txt
Search SHARED:vscsi/kick/vscsitest.txt "tests passed"
Search SHARED:vscsi/kick/vscsitest.txt FAIL
Info DH0:
Echo "kick-check done"
